# Python standards (MBS)

Adapted from [awesome-cursorrules](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules)
Python best-practices / projects guides; aligned with `AGENTS.md` and
`pyproject.toml`.

## Layout and tooling

- Package code under `src/mbs/`; tests under `tests/` (unit / integration).
- Manage deps with **uv** (`pyproject.toml` + `uv.lock`); never invent
  `requirements.txt` as the source of truth.
- Lint/format with **ruff**; typecheck with **pyright**; test with **pytest**.
- Use `pathlib.Path`; no string path concatenation.
- Production logic in `src/`; notebooks only call package functions.
- Do not edit `vendor/`; pin reference code by commit SHA elsewhere.

## Style and typing

- Target Python 3.11+; annotate public functions and dataclasses (incl. `-> None`).
- Prefer `X | None` over `Optional[X]`; use modern `collections.abc` types.
- snake_case / PascalCase / UPPER_CASE per PEP 8; line length 100 (ruff).
- Prefer absolute imports from `mbs.*`.
- Raise explicit errors on manifest, coordinate, genome-build, or checkpoint
  mismatches; never silently clip methylation or drop samples.

## CLI and config

- Extend the existing **Typer** app in `mbs.cli`; do not advertise stub commands
  as implemented.
- Resolve paths via `mbs.paths` / `$MBS_*`; all artifacts stay under `/data`.
